Fix device-thread holding the context mutex while sleeping.

The ALdc device thread calls ThreadPass() (thd_sleep(10) on Dreamcast)
while still holding the context mutex (SCOPED_LOCK(&ctx->mutex)). Every
main-thread AL call that resolves a source (_alSource()) locks the same
context mutex, so the game blocks behind those sleeps whenever any sound
plays (65 allocated sources -> ~650ms of context-mutex hold per cycle,
game becomes unplayable).

Drop the per-source ThreadPass() so the lock is only held for the brief
_updateSource() call; the usleep(5000) at the end of the cycle still
yields the device thread.

--- a/src/context.c
+++ b/src/context.c
@@ -465,9 +465,8 @@ static void* _alDeviceThread(void* dev) {
                 for(int j = 0; j < MAX_SOURCES_PER_CONTEXT; ++j) {
                     SCOPED_LOCK(&ctx->mutex);
                     Source* s = &ctx->sources[j];
                     if(!s->is_dead) {
                         _alUpdateSource(s);
-                        ThreadPass();
                     }
                 }
 
                 usleep(5000);